James inquired about designating a portion of his estate for flexible charitable distribution rather than specifying organizations, highlighting an estimated 10% bequest of $60k–$120k. I explained options such as allowing the executor discretion, creating a charitable trust, or using a community foundation, emphasizing the importance of flexibility in long-term charitable intent. We discussed practical considerations, including naming alternates and ensuring enforceability.

James then asked about selecting a guardian for his children. I advised naming his parents as first-choice guardians if they are willing and able, while also designating younger alternates. I urged revisiting the decision regularly and framing it around immediate and long-term needs. I suggested separating the guardian and trustee roles and emphasized the importance of a nonbinding letter of wishes to guide future guardianship in line with his values. Ultimately, I encouraged making a deliberate choice now and updating as needed.
